sharedSurface.types:
src/types.ts additions the dashboard reads (owners in brackets):

// Branch.apps[group] (scheduler WP + limits WP)
apps: Record<string, { image: string; port: number; url: string; updatedAt?: number; desiredState?: 'running'|'stopped'|'suspended';
  alwaysOn?: boolean;               // PUT …/always-on; default from INSTA_OSS_ALWAYS_ON_DEFAULT (false)
  limits?: { cpu: number; memoryMb: number }; // PUT …/limits -> --cpus/--memory
  sleptAt?: number | null;          // set by the idle sweep / eviction when it docker-stops a RUNNING-intent service; cleared on wake/start/deploy. Distinguishes 'standby' from 'crashed' in runtimeHealth.
}>
// Branch (scheduler WP)
dbAlwaysOn?: boolean;               // PATCH /database/settings {scaleToZero: !x}; GET /database/instance echoes scaleToZero = !dbAlwaysOn
dbSleptAt?: number | null;
dbLimits?: { cpuMilli: number; memoryMib: number }; // PATCH /database/settings {cpu:'2', memory:'4Gi'}
managed?: Record<string, { password: string; alwaysOn?: boolean; sleptAt?: number | null; limits?: { cpu: number; memoryMb: number } }>
// Project (router WP)
domains?: Array<{ hostname: string; branch: string; group: string; addedAt: number }>
// State (identity WP), src/state.ts
auth?: { admin?: { email: string; name?: string; passwordHash: string; salt: string; createdAt: number };
         sessions: Record<string /*token*/, { expiresAt: number; createdAt: number }>;
         tokens: Array<{ id: string; name: string; prefix: string; hash: string; scopes: string[]; createdAt: string; lastUsedAt: string|null; expiresAt: string|null; revokedAt: string|null }> }

Wire shapes the UI consumes (all cloud shapes):
- services[] rows (engine.services, src/engine.ts:413-470): add always_on (compute + managed), image, port (compute; cloud Service.image/port openapi.yaml:326+), template_code/template_logo_url (optional, from the template-deployment record), domain = bare host[:port] (cloud 'default access domain (postgres/compute)'), endpoint = full URL for compute ('https://web-shop-main.<domain>' or 'http://web-shop-main.localhost:<port>' in local mode) and 'host:port' for postgres/managed, '<bucket>.s3.<domain>' for storage.
- runtime-health rows (src/engine.ts:718-750): status 'standby' when the container is exited AND (desiredState != 'running' OR sleptAt is set); 'crashed' only when exited, desired running and sleptAt is null; 'starting' while a wake is in flight (scheduler marks wakingSince).
- GET /me in server mode without a session: 401 { error: 'setup required' } when state.auth.admin is absent, else 401 { error: 'unauthorized' } (cloud Error shape openapi.yaml:61-66); 200 { user, via:'jwt'|'api' } with a session or insta_ bearer; local mode unchanged (src/server.ts:55).
- POST /auth/signup in server mode: 200 {} (status is optional in the cloud schema, platform server.ts:634) when no admin exists and the password has 8+ chars; 403 { error } once an admin exists; 400 on validation. No session is created (the UI logs in next).
- POST /auth/login: 200 AuthResult (accessToken, refreshToken, expiresIn, user) AND Set-Cookie: instad_session=<accessToken>; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Secure when the request arrived over https (x-forwarded-proto from the edge). POST /auth/logout: { ok: true } and clears the cookie. The bearer check accepts Authorization: Bearer <session|insta_ token> OR the cookie.
- GET /templates -> { templates: TemplateListItem[] } with code, version, maintainer, source, name, tagline, category, tags, logoUrl (recommend a data: URI built from templates/<code>/logo.svg|png, else null), license, updatedAt, totalProjects/activeProjects/successRate/deploymentCount/activeDeploymentCount (0/0/null/0/0 locally). GET /templates/:code -> { template: TemplateDetail } with services map, variables.{required,optional}: TemplateVariable[] {name, description, required, default, generate, editable}, readme, documentationUrl, upstream.
- POST /projects/:id/template-deployments -> 202 { deploymentId, deployment } or 202 { status:'approval_required', action, approvalId }; 400 { error:'missing_variables', missing:[{name,key,description}] }. GET /template-deployments/:id -> TemplateDeployment { id, status: running|succeeded|failed|partial, step: create_services|write_variables|deploy|health_check, templateCode, templateVersion, projectId, branchId, services:[{name, serviceId, url, state: pending|created|deployed|healthy|failed}], error?, logsTail?, createdAt }.
- GET /projects/:id/compute/domains?branch&group -> { items: DomainResult[] }; DomainResult = { hostname, flyApp (the daemon puts the container name), configured, status: 'pending'|'active'|'error'|'not added', dns: [{ type:'CNAME'|'A', name, value, note?, status?: 'ok'|'missing'|'mismatch' }], service, region: 'local', ssl?: 'pending'|'issued', errorReason?, origin?, originOk? }.
